{"name":"Sycamore Tree","hex":"#3f544f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sycamore tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of the genus Platanus"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sycamore_tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sycamore Tree (Santa Paula, California)","blocks":[{"text":"The Sycamore Tree is a historic tree used for many years as a special meeting place.\nThe tree is located just off California State Route 126 in the middle of Hall Road, 4 Miles East of Santa Paula, California in Ventura County. Address is in the 3800 block of Sycamore Road, Fillmore, California, just north of the Santa Clara River. The site became California Historical Landmark number 756 on February 22, 1960. The tree has been used in the past as a polling place, Padres resting place on the El Camino Real, outdoor chapel and post office. In December 1846 General John C. Frémont passed the tree on his trip to sign a treaty with General Andrés Pico to secure California's annexation to the United States, called the Treaty of Cahuenga. The Treaty was signed on January 13, 1847, at Campo de Cahuenga in what is now Universal City, California."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b4/JohnCFremont-1856.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sycamore_Tree_(Santa_Paula%2C_California)","wikidata":"Q104875900"},{"title":"Sycamore","blocks":[{"text":"Sycamore is a name which has been applied to several types of trees, but with somewhat similar leaf forms. The name derives from the Ancient Greek σῡκόμορος meaning 'fig-mulberry'."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sycamore","wikidata":"Q3506777"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg/500px-Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg/1280px-Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg/500px-Campo_de_Cahuenga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Campo de Cahuenga, scene of the signing of the Treaty of Cahuenga","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACampo_de_Cahuenga.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Andres_Pico.jpg/500px-Andres_Pico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Andres_Pico.jpg/500px-Andres_Pico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Andrés Pico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndres_Pico.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/500px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg/1280px-Larix_decidua_Aletschwald.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_